              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daintree_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Daintree National Park\">Daintree National Park</a></b> is a national park in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_North_Queensland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Far North Queensland\">Far North Queensland</a>, Australia, 1,757 km (1,092 mi) northwest of Brisbane and 100 km (62 mi) northwest of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cairns\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Cairns\">Cairns</a>. It was founded in 1981 and is part of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wet_Tropics_of_Queensland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Wet Tropics of Queensland\">Wet Tropics of Queensland</a>.  In 1988 it became a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Heritage_Site\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:World Heritage Site\">World Heritage Site</a>. The park consists of two sections, with a settled agricultural area between them which includes the towns of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mossman,_Queensland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Mossman, Queensland\">Mossman</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daintree,_Queensland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Daintree, Queensland\">Daintree Village</a>.",
